0 for jets originating from gluons and light-flavour quarks (light jets) and about 6 for jets induced by charm quarks, determined using MC simulated $t\\bar{t}$ events.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "The events used by the search described in this paper were selected using a trigger logic that accepts events with a missing transverse momentum above $70$ – $110\\penalty 10000\\ \text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}$ , depending on the data-taking period.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "The events used by the search described in this paper were selected using a trigger logic that accepts events with a missing transverse momentum above $70$ – $110\\penalty 10000\\ \text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}$ , depending on the data-taking period.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The events used by the search described in this paper were selected using a trigger logic that accepts events with a missing transverse momentum above $70$ – $110\\penalty 10000\\ \text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}$ , depending on the data-taking period."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + The ATLAS detector and data samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the context of the trigger logic used to select events for the search, and in the description of the physics objects.\", \"quote\": \"The events used by the search described in this paper were selected using a trigger logic that accepts events with a missing transverse momentum above $70$ – $110\\penalty 10000\\ \\text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}$ , depending on the data-taking period.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "The events used by the search described in this paper were sel