{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2201.11585", "answer": null, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 fb−1 of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at √s=13 TeV and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 fb−1 of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at √s=13 TeV and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 fb−1 of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at √s=13 TeV and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson.\", \"quote\": \"A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 fb−1 of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at √s=13 TeV and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 $\\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 $\\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion.\", \"quote\": \"A search for invisible decays of the Higgs boson produced via vector boson fusion (VBF) has been performed with 101 $\\,\\text{fb}^{-1}$ of proton-proton collisions delivered by the LHC at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and collected by the CMS detector in 2017 and 2018.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": null, "quote": "The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quark jets with ${p_{\\mathrm{T}}>20\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}}$ and ${\\lvert\\eta\rvert<2.4}$ with 68% efficiency, and 1.1 (12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon ( $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ quark) jet as a bottom quark jet.", "unanimous": false, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets or any similar technique for identifying jets containing a b-hadron.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets or any process involving b-hadron identification.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Data and simulated samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various simulation and generation processes for different particles and events, but it does not mention the use of b-tagged jets in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Data and simulated samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various simulation methods and processes used in the analysis, but it does not mention the use of b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quark jets with ${p_{\\mathrm{T}}>20\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}}$ and ${\\lvert\\eta\rvert<2.4}$ with 68% efficiency, and 1.1 (12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon ( $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ quark) jet as a bottom quark jet.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quark jets with ${p_{\\mathrm{T}}>20\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}}$ and ${\\lvert\\eta\rvert<2.4}$ with 68% efficiency, and 1.1 (12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon ( $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ quark) jet as a bottom quark jet."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of the DeepCSV algorithm to tag b quark jets with specific efficiency and misidentification rates.\", \"quote\": \"The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quark jets with ${p_{\\mathrm{T}}>20\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}}$ and ${\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4}$ with 68% efficiency, and 1.1 (12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon ( $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ quark) jet as a bottom quark jet.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag b quark jets with pT>20 GeV and |η|<2.4 with 68% efficiency, and 1.1(12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon (c quark) jet as a bottom quark jet.", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of the DeepCSV algorithm to tag b-quark jets, but it does not explicitly state that b-tagged jets are used in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"The specific features of heavy-flavored jets, in particular the presence of displaced vertices, are used in a multivariate jet tagging method. The “medium” working point of the DeepCSV algorithm from Ref. [ 63 ] is used to tag b quark jets with pT>20 GeV and |η|<2.4 with 68% efficiency, and 1.1(12)% probability of misidentifying a light-flavor or gluon (c quark) jet as a bottom quark jet.\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": null, "quote": "The final state for this analysis is composed solely of jets from gluons or light-flavored quarks, and missing transverse momentum.", "unanimous": false, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the context of trigger strategies and sensitivity, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires it.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that the trigger strategy in the previous CMS publication required a high threshold on the missing transverse momentum, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection in this analysis requires missing transverse momentum.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2201.11585", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "sectio