lysis is a search for a new neutral gauge boson, Z', produced in association with one or two jets, including at least one b jet, and decaying into a pair of muons.\",\n  \"quote\": \"A search for a new neutral gauge boson, Z', produced in association with one or two jets, including at least one b jet, and decaying into a pair of muons is presented.\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that the analysis searches for a Z' boson produced in association with one or more jets where at least one is b tagged, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that the search is for a Z' boson produced in association with one or more jets where at least one is b-tagged. However, it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the identification of jets containing b quarks using the DeepJet algorithm and specifies the requirements for b-tagged jets.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged.\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly mentions the use of b-tagged jets in the event selection process.\", \"quote\": \"Jets containing b quarks can be identified utilizing the relatively long b quark lifetime and identifying a secondary vertex within the jet, as well as using jet shape variables [ 51 ] . We utilize the medium working point of the DeepJet algorithm [ 52 , 53 ] defined by a 1% misidentification probability for jets originated from light-quarks or gluons, yielding an efficiency of $\\approx 90\\%$ to identify jets originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quarks as $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": null, "quote": "Further requirements to suppress backgrounds beyond the selections introduced in Section 2 depend on the dilepton invariant mass $m_{{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}}$ and the jet multiplicity. Consequently, two-dimensional Bottom Quark Fusion (BQF) variable selections are applied to optimize the analysis as a function of the reconstructed dilepton mass. These are upper bounds on $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}/m$ and on the difference between the scalar sum of jet transverse momenta ( $H_{\\mathrm{T}}$ ) and lepton transverse momenta ( $L_{\\mathrm{T}}$ ), denoted as $H_{\\mathrm{T}}-L_{\\mathrm{T}}$ .", "unanimous": false, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the search for a new neutral gauge boson produced in association with one or two b jets and decaying into a pair of muons. It does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the event selection criteria.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the context of event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the computation of the missing transverse momentum vector and its magnitude, but it does not mention using it as a requirement for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the computation of the missing transverse momentum vector ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mkern 3.0mu\\text{miss}}$ and its magnitude $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$, but it does not explicitly state that this quantity is used in the event selection criteria.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "Further requirements to suppress backgrounds beyond the selections introduced in Section 2 depend on the dilepton invariant mass $m_{{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}}$ and the jet multiplicity. Consequently, two-dimensional Bottom Quark Fusion (BQF) variable selections are applied to optimize the analysis as a function of the reconstructed dilepton mass. These are upper bounds on $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}/m$ and on the difference between the scalar sum of jet transverse momenta ( $H_{\\mathrm{T}}$ ) and lepton transverse momenta ( $L_{\\mathrm{T}}$ ), denoted as $H_{\\mathrm{T}}-L_{\\mathrm{T}}$ .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Further requirements to suppress backgrounds beyond the selections introduced in Section 2 depend on the dilepton invariant mass $m_{{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}}$ and the jet multiplicity. Consequently, two-dimensional Bottom Quark Fusion (BQF) variable selections are applied to optimize the analysis as a function of the reconstructed dilepton mass. These are upper bounds on $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}/m$ and on the difference between the scalar sum of jet transverse momenta ( $H_{\\mathrm{T}}$ ) and lepton transverse momenta