{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2112.03161", "answer": null, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons.\", \"quote\": \"A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons, which indicates a search for new physics.\",\n  \"quote\": \"A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": null, "quote": "Identifying the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ decay in signal events and discriminating against background events relies on tagging jets as likely to have originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ hadron decays.", "unanimous": false, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes the search for heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons and mentions specific decay channels involving bottom quarks and leptons, but it does not explicitly state that b-tagged jets are used in the event selection.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the search for heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons, with one Higgs boson decaying into a bottom quark pair and the other into final states with leptons. It does not mention the use of b-tagged jets in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of b-tagging algorithms for identifying jets with b-hadrons, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of b-tagging algorithms for identifying jets with b-hadrons, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and global event reconstruction + Simulated samples + Decay chain reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the event selection process and the use of various triggers, but it does not mention the use of b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and global event reconstruction + Simulated samples + Decay chain reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the CMS detector, event reconstruction, and simulated samples, but it does not mention the use of b-tagged jets in the event selection process.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Identifying the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ decay in signal events and discriminating against background events relies on tagging jets as likely to have originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ hadron decays.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Identifying the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ decay in signal events and discriminating against background events relies on tagging jets as likely to have originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ hadron decays."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Electron and muon identification + Reconstruction and flavor identification of jets + Reconstructing the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ system mass", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of a DeepAK8 mass-decorrelated Z/H to bb tagger for identifying jets consistent with a bb decay, which is a form of b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"Identifying the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ decay in signal events and discriminating against background events relies on tagging jets as likely to have originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ hadron decays.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Electron and muon identification + Reconstruction and flavor identification of jets + Reconstructing the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ system mass", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the identification of jets as containing b-hadrons using a specific tagger, but it does not explicitly state that b-tagged jets are used in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}>85\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the search for heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons in specific final states involving leptons and a bottom quark pair, but it does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) as a requirement for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the search for heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons and the final states considered, but it does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) as a requirement for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "In the single-lepton (SL) channel, the quarks in the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\to{\\mathup{{{W}}}}{\\mathup{{{W}}}}^{*}\to\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}{\\mathup{}}{\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}$ decay are reconstructed as a single large jet (the ${\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}~\text{jet}$ ) with a nearby lepton ( $\\mathup{{{e}}}$ or ). This jet is required to have substructure consistent with a decay to two energetic quarks. This Higgs boson decay chain is reconstructed as the ${\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}~\text{jet}$ , the lepton, and the missing transverse momentum ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ .", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum in the context of event reconstruction but does not explicitly state that it is a requirement for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"In the single-lepton (SL) channel, the quarks in the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{W}}}}{\\mathup{{{W}}}}^{*}\\to\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}{\\mathup{}}{\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}$ decay are reconstructed as a single large jet (the ${\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}~\\text{jet}$ ) with a nearby lepton ( $\\mathup{{{e}}}$ or ). This jet is required to have substructure consistent with a decay to two energetic quarks. This Higgs boson decay chain is reconstructed as the ${\\mathup{{{q}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{q}}}}}}}}}^{\\prime}~\\text{jet}$ , the lepton, and the missing transverse momentum ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ .\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the context of event reconstruction, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires it.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and global event reconstruction + Simulated samples + Decay chain reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes the computation of missing transverse momentum (pTmiss) but does not mention its use in event selection.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and global event reconstruction + Simulated samples + Decay chain reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the computation of the vector pTmiss and its magnitude, denoted as pTmiss, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires missing transverse momentum.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Electron and muon identification + Reconstruction and flavor identification of jets + Reconstructing the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ system mass", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the selection criteria for leptons, jets, and the reconstruction of the Higgs boson system mass, but it does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss).\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Electron and muon identification + Reconstruction and flavor identification of jets + Reconstructing the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ system mass", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the event selection criteria for leptons, jet reconstruction, and the identification of Higgs boson decays, but it does not mention missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss).\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Single-lepton channel + Dilepton channel", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ as an input for the likelihood-based technique in the single-lepton channel and as a direct component for the dilepton channel, but it does not explicitly state that missing transverse momentum is a requirement for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "The observable pTmiss is the missing transverse momentum.", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Single-lepton channel + Dilepton channel", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the use of missing transverse momentum (pTmiss) in the analysis, specifically in the likelihood function and the reconstruction of the Higgs boson four-momentum.\", \"quote\": \"The observable pTmiss is the missing transverse momentum.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}>85\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}>85\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$"], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization + Single-lepton channel event selection + Dilepton channel event selection", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that the dilepton channel event selection requires $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}>85\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\", \"quote\": \"Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}>85\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.03161", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "Thus, we also require that $\\lvert\\Delta\\phi({\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}},\\vec{p}_{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}})\rvert<\\pi/2$ to discriminate against ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}/\\gamma^{*}\\!\\!+\\!\text{jets}$ . Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}>85\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Thus, we also require that $\\lvert\\Delta\\phi({\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}},\\vec{p}_{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}})\rvert<\\pi/2$ to discriminate against ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}/\\gamma^{*}\\!\\!+\\!\text{jets}$ . Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}>85\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization + Single-lepton channel event selection + Dilepton channel event selection", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the requirement for missing transverse momentum (pTmiss) in the dilepton channel event selection.\", \"quote\": \"Thus, we also require that $\\lvert\\Delta\\phi({\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}},\\vec{p}_{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}})\\rvert<\\pi/2$ to discriminate against ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}/\\gamma^{*}\\!\\!+\\!\\text{jets}$ . Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}>85\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ .\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}}, "missing": ["Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?"], "quotes": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": "A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented.", "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": "Identifying the ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ decay in signal events and discriminating against background events relies on tagging jets as likely to have originated from $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ hadron decays.", "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": "Background is further separated from signal by requiring $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}>85\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$"}, "quote": "A search for new heavy resonances decaying to a pair of Higgs bosons ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ ) in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV is presented."}
