lation in this coupling and measurements of the production rate of the Higgs boson, via its decay into two photons, in association with top quarks."}
{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2011.07812", "answer": false, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CLs prescription.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This Letter addresses that gap in coverage.", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses a search for displaced leptons in pp collisions, which is a signature of long-lived particles that could indicate new physics beyond the Standard Model.\", \"quote\": \"This Letter addresses that gap in coverage.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This Letter addresses that gap in coverage.", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses a search for particles with long lifetimes, which are a feature of both the Standard Model and theories beyond the Standard Model. It specifically mentions searching for displaced leptons, which are not identified by previous ATLAS searches.\", \"quote\": \"This Letter addresses that gap in coverage.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9 +  + Body ¶10 + Body ¶11 + Body ¶12 + Body ¶13", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the analysis of signal regions and background estimations using various methods, but it does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9 +  + Body ¶10 + Body ¶11 + Body ¶12 + Body ¶13", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes the analysis of background events and the estimation of background contributions using various methods, but it does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CLs prescription.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CLs prescription."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶14 +  + Body ¶15 + Body ¶16 + Body ¶17 + Body ¶18 + Body ¶19 + Body ¶20", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the evaluation of systematic uncertainties, the comparison of data and simulation, and the derivation of exclusion limits on $\\tilde{\\ell}$ masses. It mentions the use of the CLs prescription and the HistFitter package for statistical interpretation, indicating a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CLs prescription.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CL ${}_{\\text{s}}$ prescription [ 82 ] .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\\tilde{\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CL ${}_{\\text{s}}$ prescription [ 82 ] ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶14 +  + Body ¶15 + Body ¶16 + Body ¶17 + Body ¶18 + Body ¶19 + Body ¶20", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the analysis of signal systematic uncertainties, background predictions, and exclusion limits on $\\\\tilde{\\\\ell}$ masses, indicating a search for new physics rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity.\", \"quote\": \"As no excess of events is observed, exclusion limits on the $\\\\tilde{\\\\ell}$ masses are derived at 95% confidence level (CL) following the CL ${}_{\\\\text{s}}$ prescription [ 82 ] .\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": false, "quote": "", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the event selection criteria for displaced leptons, including requirements for transverse impact parameter, transverse momentum, and isolation from nearby activity. It does not mention the use of b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Bo