": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "SMEFT interpretation", "window": 14, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes an analysis using the Standard Model effective field theory (SMEFT) to interpret data, focusing on dimension-6 operators and their Wilson coefficients. It discusses various fitting scenarios and the sensitivity of different observables to these operators, but does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "SMEFT interpretation", "window": 15, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes measurements of the fiducial $t\\bar{t}Z$ cross section and various normalised differential distributions, and it reports numerical values and constraints on Wilson coefficients in the context of SMEFT. It does not mention searching for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "SMEFT interpretation", "window": 15, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses measurements of differential distributions and fits to EFT operators, but does not explicitly state that it is searching for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "SMEFT interpretation", "window": 16, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the analysis of effective field theory (EFT) directions of sensitivity and presents results from a linearised Fisher-rotated fit, but it does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "SMEFT interpretation", "window": 16, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the interpretation of the analysis within the framework of the Standard Model Effective Field Theory (SMEFT) and presents results related to various Wilson coefficients and their combinations. It does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Conclusion", "window": 17, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes measurements of cross sections and differential production cross sections for t t-bar Z production, comparisons with Standard Model predictions, and constraints on Beyond the Standard Model (BSM) effects using Effective Field Theory (EFT). It does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "Templates from simulated t t-bar Z events, generated with and without the SM spin density matrix, are used to extract a fraction f SM =1.20±0.68 reflecting the strength of spin correlations like those in the SM in t t-bar Z data events, with the uncertainty largely dominated by its statistical component.", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Conclusion", "window": 17, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes measurements of cross sections and differential production cross sections for t t-bar Z production, and compares these measurements to Standard Model predictions. It also mentions searching for spin correlations and constraining potential BSM effects using EFT operators, but these are not the primary focus of the analysis.\", \"quote\": \"Templates from simulated t t-bar Z events, generated with and without the SM spin density matrix, are used to extract a fraction f SM =1.20±0.68 reflecting the strength of spin correlations like those in the SM in t t-bar Z data events, with the uncertainty largely dominated by its statistical component.\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 18, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various measurements of the inclusive $t\\bar{t}Z$ cross section and differential cross sections, including the unfolding procedure and comparisons with MC predictions. It does not mention any search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 18, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various measurements of the inclusive t tbar Z cross section and differential cross sections, as well as details of the unfolding procedure and comparisons with MC generators. It does not mention searching for new physics.\",\n \"quote\": \"\",\n \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 19, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various cross-section measurements of different observables, such as $|\\Delta\\Phi(Z,t_{\\mathrm{lep}})|/\\pi$, $H_{\\text{T}}^{\\ell}$, $N_{\\mathrm{jets}}$, etc., in different channels. There is no mention of searching for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 19, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes various cross-section measurements of different observables in the 3ℓ and 4ℓ channels, unfolded to particle level and parton level. It also includes compatibility tests with various predictions. There is no mention of a search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 20, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search for new physics or a measurement of a Standard Model quantity.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 20, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search for new physics, nor does it mention any specific Standard Model quantity being measured.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2312.04450", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Appendix", "window": 21, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search for new physics, nor does 