{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2004.14060", "answer": true, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents a search for top squark pair production", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents a search for top squark pair production", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["This paper presents a search for top squark pair production"], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the paper presents a search for top squark pair production, which is a new physics scenario beyond the Standard Model.\", \"quote\": \"This paper presents a search for top squark pair production\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents a search for top squark pair production with an experimental signature of at least two jets, large missing transverse momentum, and no electrons or muons, using 139 fb−1 of proton–proton ( pp ) collision data provided by the LHC at a centre-of-mass energy of √s=13 TeV and collected by the ATLAS detector in 2015–2018.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["This paper presents a search for top squark pair production with an experimental signature of at least two jets, large missing transverse momentum, and no electrons or muons, using 139 fb−1 of proton–proton ( pp ) collision data provided by the LHC at a centre-of-mass energy of √s=13 TeV and collected by the ATLAS detector in 2015–2018."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the paper presents a search for top squark pair production, which is a new physics scenario beyond the Standard Model.\",\n  \"quote\": \"This paper presents a search for top squark pair production with an experimental signature of at least two jets, large missing transverse momentum, and no electrons or muons, using 139 fb−1 of proton–proton ( pp ) collision data provided by the LHC at a centre-of-mass energy of √s=13 TeV and collected by the ATLAS detector in 2015–2018.\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "Jets which contain b-hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance (|η|<2.5) are identified as ‘b-tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of b- and c-hadrons inside the jet [39].", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions improved identification efficiencies for jets containing b-hadrons, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the search for a scalar partner of the top quark and the methods used for event selection, including the use of techniques to identify jets containing b-hadrons, but it does not explicitly state that b-tagged jets are used in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Data collection and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the efficiency of identifying jets containing b-hadrons (b-jets) and the probability of mis-tagging jets containing only charm hadrons (c-jets) and only lighter hadrons (light-flavour jets), but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Data collection and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions the efficiency of identifying jets containing b-hadrons (b-jets), but it does not explicitly state that the event selection uses b-tagged jets.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Jets which contain b-hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance (|η|<2.5) are identified as ‘b-tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of b- and c-hadrons inside the jet [39].", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Jets which contain b-hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance (|η|<2.5) are identified as ‘b-tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of b- and c-hadrons inside the jet [39]."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the identification of jets containing b-hadrons and the use of a multivariate algorithm for b-tagging.\", \"quote\": \"Jets which contain b-hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance (|η|<2.5) are identified as ‘b-tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of b- and c-hadrons inside the jet [39].\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Jets which contain $b$ -hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance ( $|\\eta|<2.5$ ) are identified as ‘ $b$ -tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters 3 3 3 The transverse impact parameter, $d_{0}$ , is defined as the distance of closest approach of a track to the beam-line, measured in the transverse plane. The longitudinal impact parameter, $z_{0}$ , corresponds to the $z$ -coordinate distance between the point along the track at which the transverse impact parameter is defined and the primary vertex. of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of $b$ - and $c$ -hadrons inside the jet [ 39 ] .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Jets which contain $b$ -hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance ( $|\\eta|<2.5$ ) are identified as ‘ $b$ -tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters 3 3 3 The transverse impact parameter, $d_{0}$ , is defined as the distance of closest approach of a track to the beam-line, measured in the transverse plane. The longitudinal impact parameter, $z_{0}$ , corresponds to the $z$ -coordinate distance between the point along the track at which the transverse impact parameter is defined and the primary vertex. of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of $b$ - and $c$ -hadrons inside the jet [ 39 ] ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the identification of jets containing b-hadrons and refers to them as 'b-tagged' jets.\", \"quote\": \"Jets which contain $b$ -hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance ( $|\\eta|<2.5$ ) are identified as ‘ $b$ -tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters 3 3 3 The transverse impact parameter, $d_{0}$ , is defined as the distance of closest approach of a track to the beam-line, measured in the transverse plane. The longitudinal impact parameter, $z_{0}$ , corresponds to the $z$ -coordinate distance between the point along the track at which the transverse impact parameter is defined and the primary vertex. of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of $b$ - and $c$ -hadrons inside the jet [ 39 ] .\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "Selected events are required to pass a missing transverse momentum (whose magnitude is denoted by $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ ) trigger [ 67 ] , which is fully efficient for events with reconstructed $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}>250$ GeV", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions 'large missing transverse momentum' as part of the experimental signature, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires missing transverse momentum.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.14060", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "q