econstruction ).", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Selected events are required to pass a missing transverse momentum (whose magnitude is denoted by $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ ) trigger [ 67 ] , which is fully efficient for events with reconstructed $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}>250$ GeV (the $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ reconstruction is described in Section Event reconstruction )."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Data collection and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly mentions that events are required to pass a missing transverse momentum trigger, which is fully efficient for events with reconstructed $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}>250$ GeV.\", \"quote\": \"Selected events are required to pass a missing transverse momentum (whose magnitude is denoted by $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ ) trigger [ 67 ] , which is fully efficient for events with reconstructed $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}>250$ GeV (the $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ reconstruction is described in Section Event reconstruction ).\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}}, "missing": [], "quotes": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": "This paper presents a search for top squark pair production", "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": "Jets which contain b-hadrons and are within the inner-detector acceptance (|η|<2.5) are identified as ‘b-tagged’ using a multivariate algorithm that exploits the impact parameters of the charged-particle tracks, the presence of secondary vertices, and the reconstructed flight paths of b- and c-hadrons inside the jet [39].", "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": "Selected events are required to pass a missing transverse momentum (whose magnitude is denoted by $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}$ ) trigger [ 67 ] , which is fully efficient for events with reconstructed $E_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\mathrm{miss}}>250$ GeV"}, "quote": "This paper presents a search for top squark pair production", "quote_supports": true, "support_why": "The first sentence confirms the analysis is a search (not a measurement). The second sentence explicitly describes the use of b-tagged jets in event selection. The third sentence requires missing transverse momentum (E_T^miss) as a trigger condition. Together, they satisfy all parts of the criteria.", "judged_by": "Qwen/QwQ-32B-AWQ"}
