{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2001.06899", "answer": false, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": false, "quote": "", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes measurements of cross section ratios involving Z bosons and charm or bottom quark jets, comparing these with theoretical predictions and previous measurements, but does not mention searching for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that it measures cross section ratios of Z boson production with charm or bottom quark jets, and compares these measurements with pQCD calculations. It does not mention searching for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes the reconstruction and selection of events involving Z bosons and jets, focusing on the identification of heavy-flavor jets. It does not mention searching for new physics.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the reconstruction and selection of Z+jets events, including detailed procedures for identifying electrons, muons, and jets, and the application of various selection criteria. It does not mention any search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the selection criteria and background processes for Z+jets and Z+HF jets samples, including the numbers of events and uncertainties. It does not mention any search for new physics.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the reconstruction of objects and event selection criteria, and provides tables of event counts for different processes, including Z+jets and Z+HF jets. It does not mention searching for new physics or any deviations from Standard Model predictions.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Cross section ratio measurements + Analysis strategy + $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ +HF jets event tagging efficiency", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes a measurement of the fraction of jets with heavy flavors in Z+jets events and the calculation of cross section ratios, which are Standard Model quantities.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Cross section ratio measurements + Analysis strategy + $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ +HF jets event tagging efficiency", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes a measurement of the fraction of jets with heavy flavors in ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ events and the calculation of cross section ratios, which are Standard Model quantities.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Estimation of the event yields", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes a method to estimate the event yields of Z+c jets and Z+b jets using a binned maximum likelihood template fit, which involves adjusting Monte Carlo rates to fit the data. It also mentions the validation of the c jet M_SV shape and the correction of the b jet M_SV templates. However, there is no mention of searching for new physics.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Estimation of the event yields", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes a method to estimate the yields of Z+c jets and Z+b jets events using a binned maximum likelihood template fit based on M_SV distributions. It does not mention searching for new physics.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"pap