{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2006.05880", "answer": false, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents the results of a search for top squarks in final states with Higgs or Z bosons at √s=13 TeV using the complete data sample collected with the ATLAS detector [ 19 ] in proton–proton ( pp ) collisions during Run-2 of the LHC (2015–2018), corresponding to 139 fb -1 .", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents the results of a search for top squarks in final states with Higgs or Z bosons at √s=13 TeV using the complete data sample collected with the ATLAS detector [ 19 ] in proton–proton ( pp ) collisions during Run-2 of the LHC (2015–2018), corresponding to 139 fb -1 .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["This paper presents the results of a search for top squarks in final states with Higgs or Z bosons at √s=13 TeV using the complete data sample collected with the ATLAS detector [ 19 ] in proton–proton ( pp ) collisions during Run-2 of the LHC (2015–2018), corresponding to 139 fb -1 ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for top squarks, which are new physics particles beyond the Standard Model.\",\n  \"quote\": \"This paper presents the results of a search for top squarks in final states with Higgs or Z bosons at √s=13 TeV using the complete data sample collected with the ATLAS detector [ 19 ] in proton–proton ( pp ) collisions during Run-2 of the LHC (2015–2018), corresponding to 139 fb -1 .\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "This paper presents the results of a search for top squarks in final states with Higgs or Z bosons at √s=13 TeV u