{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2508.13900", "answer": true, "conditions": {"Is this paper a SEARCH for new physics, rather than a measurement of a Standard Model quantity?": {"answer": true, "quote": "A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis is a search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra, which is a search for new physics beyond the Standard Model.\", \"quote\": \"A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c0", "answer": true, "quote": "A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes a search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra, focusing on events with significant missing transverse momentum and initial-state-radiation jets.\", \"quote\": \"A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables.\", \"quote\": \"Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c1", "answer": true, "quote": "Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables.\", \"quote\": \"Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}]}, "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": {"answer": true, "quote": "events are selected based on significant ISR activity that causes the sparticle system to recoil resulting in observable $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ from the momentum received by the invisible sparticles.", "unanimous": true, "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the context of the approach taken for the search, but does not explicitly state that the event selection requires it.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses the selection of events with significant initial-state radiation (ISR) and mentions that the high transverse momentum recoil from the ISR can lead to measurable missing transverse momentum. However, it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss).\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions that missing transverse momentum is considered as a physics object and describes how it is calculated and used in event filters, but it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires missing transverse momentum.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) as a physics object considered in the analysis and describes how it is defined and modified. However, it does not explicitly state that the event selection requires missing transverse momentum.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Signal and background simulation", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the simulation of signal and background processes, the generation of events, and the decay models used. It does not mention any requirement for missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the event selection process.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Signal and background simulation", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text describes the simulation of various SUSY signal and SM background processes, including the generation of events, hadronization, showering, and detector simulation. It details the specific models and decay processes considered, but does not mention the requirement for missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Signal and background simulation", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes the simulation of various backgrounds and signal processes using different generators, but it does not mention the use of missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) in the event selection.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\",\n  \"answer\": \"no\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Signal and background simulation", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text describes various background and signal simulations using different generators but does not mentio