 energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.", "Does the event selection use b-tagged jets (jets identified as containing a b-hadron)?": "Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of b-tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.", "Does the event selection require missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss)?": "events are selected based on significant ISR activity that causes the sparticle system to recoil resulting in observable $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ from the momentum received by the invisible sparticles."}, "quote": "A general search is presented for supersymmetric particles (sparticles) in scenarios featuring compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13  TeV , recorded with the CMS detector at the LHC.", "quote_supports": true, "support_why": "The first sentence confirms the analysis is a search for supersymmetric particles. The second explicitly includes 'number of b-tagged jets' in event categorization. The third states that events are selected based on observable p_T^miss from invisible sparticles. Together, they establish all required elements.", "judged_by": "Qwen/QwQ-32B-AWQ"}
