s kinematic variables and selection criteria but does not explicitly state that missing transverse momentum (MET / ETmiss / pTmiss) is required for event selection.\", \"quote\": \"\", \"answer\": \"no\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2503.19420", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "Furthermore, the $E_{\text{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Furthermore, the $E_{\text{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "$3\\ell$ channel + $4\\ell$ channel", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ as a selection criterion in the $Z$ -dominated channel and as a useful variable for separating different processes in the $Z$ -depleted channel.\", \"quote\": \"Furthermore, the $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos.\", \"answer\": \"yes\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2503.19420", "qid": "gf-01.c2", "answer": true, "quote": "Furthermore, the $E_{\text{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Furthermore, the $E_{\text{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "$3\\ell$ channel + $4\\ell$ channel", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ in the context of event selection criteria, specifically in the $Z$ -dominated channel and the $4\\ell$ channel.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Furthermore, the $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ is required to be larger than \\qty 30 GeV to select final states with neutrinos.\",\n  \"answer\": \"yes\"\n}\n```"}]}}, "missing": ["I